---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { latestVersion } from '../../data/site';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
const withBase = (path: string) => `${base}${path.replace(/^\/+/, '')}`;

const toc = [
  { id: 'install', label: 'Install ilyStream' },
  { id: 'first-launch', label: 'First launch tour' },
  { id: 'health-check', label: 'Run Health Center' },
  { id: 'connect-platforms', label: 'Connect platforms' },
  { id: 'studio', label: 'Build the studio' },
  { id: 'next-steps', label: 'Next steps' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Getting started"
  description="Install ilyStream, learn the main workspaces, run Health Center, and connect your first live platform."
  slug="getting-started"
  updated="July 2026"
  readingTime="8 min"
  toc={toc}
>
  <p>
    This is the shortest path from a fresh install to a stream-ready app. You will
    install ilyStream, learn the main sections, run Health Center, connect at least
    one platform, and verify that overlays and audio can be tested before you go live.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install">Install ilyStream</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Download the Windows installer.</strong> Grab <code>{`ilyStream-Setup-${latestVersion}.exe`}</code> from the <a href={withBase('download/')}>Download page</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Run the installer.</strong> Double-click the file. If Windows SmartScreen appears, click <em>More info</em>, then <em>Run anyway</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Launch ilyStream.</strong> Open it from the Start menu or desktop shortcut.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="callout">
    <span class="callout__icon">i</span>
    <p><strong>Portable build.</strong> Prefer no install? Download <code>{`ilyStream-Portable-${latestVersion}.exe`}</code>. Use the installer for your real stream PC unless you specifically need a throwaway portable copy.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="first-launch">First launch tour</h2>
  <p>
    ilyStream is organized by stream job, not by random settings buckets. The left
    rail switches categories, and the second rail shows pages inside the current category.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Live</strong>: Dashboard, Health Center, Broadcast Studio, Chat Hub, Audience Stats, and Recordings.</li>
    <li><strong>Connect</strong>: TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, Kick, and social integrations.</li>
    <li><strong>Create</strong>: Overlays, widgets, alert routes, soundboard, and Voice FX.</li>
    <li><strong>Automate</strong>: TTS, AI Co-Host, automation rules, song requests, and event testing.</li>
    <li><strong>Hardware</strong>: Hue, Govee, Elgato, Logitech, DeskThing, and other devices.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="health-check">Run Health Center</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Open Live &rarr; Health Center.</strong> This page summarizes platform readiness, chat capability, relay support, recent events, and current risks.</li>
    <li><strong>Click Refresh.</strong> Let ilyStream pull the latest status from every configured connector.</li>
    <li><strong>Use Open Setup on anything blocked.</strong> Fix one platform at a time instead of hunting through the app.</li>
    <li><strong>Use Chat Test or Test All Chats.</strong> Confirm that inbound chat and outbound relay paths behave before you start a stream.</li>
    <li><strong>Copy Report when troubleshooting.</strong> The report is meant to give you or a helper enough context without digging through logs first.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="connect-platforms">Connect platforms</h2>
  <p>
    Connect at least one live platform before spending time on automation. The full
    guide covers all four, but the basic flow is the same: open the platform page,
    add credentials, connect, then verify in Health Center.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>TikTok.</strong> Open <em>Connect &rarr; TikTok</em>, enter your TikTok username, and use the waiting mode so ilyStream connects automatically when you go live.</li>
    <li><strong>Twitch.</strong> Open <em>Connect &rarr; Twitch</em>, sign in with Twitch, and make sure chat read/send permissions are granted.</li>
    <li><strong>YouTube.</strong> Open <em>Connect &rarr; YouTube</em>, use Google OAuth, and paste the exact live video URL if automatic discovery is blocked by quota.</li>
    <li><strong>Kick.</strong> Open <em>Connect &rarr; Kick</em>, run the local receiver, expose it with Cloudflared, and subscribe your Kick app to events.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="callout callout--success">
    <span class="callout__icon">&check;</span>
    <p><strong>Verify after each platform.</strong> Return to Health Center after connecting a platform. If it says chat is read-only, relay buttons may stay disabled by design.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="studio">Build the studio</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Open Broadcast Studio.</strong> Add a scene, choose horizontal or dual/vertical mix, and add your capture sources.</li>
    <li><strong>Add overlays.</strong> In <em>Create &rarr; Overlays &amp; Widgets</em>, copy browser-source URLs into OBS or TikTok Live Studio as needed.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the mixer.</strong> Confirm your mic, TTS, soundboard, alerts, and master bus are visible and not clipping.</li>
    <li><strong>Test alerts.</strong> In <em>Create &rarr; Alert Routes</em>, select a route and press <em>Test alert</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Confirm Chat Hub.</strong> Open <em>Live &rarr; Chat Hub</em> and verify incoming chat appears in one feed.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="next-steps">Next steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={withBase('docs/platforms/')}>Live platform setup</a>: exact TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, and Kick steps.</li>
    <li><a href={withBase('docs/chat-relay/')}>Chat Hub &amp; relay</a>: auto-relay, manual outbound replies, and relay cleanup.</li>
    <li><a href={withBase('docs/audience-stats/')}>Audience profiles &amp; stats</a>: merged identities, primary accounts, badges, and sorting.</li>
    <li><a href={withBase('docs/alerts-widgets/')}>Alerts &amp; widgets</a>: browser sources, event routes, and test alerts.</li>
    <li><a href={withBase('docs/audio-tts/')}>Audio routing &amp; TTS</a>: command filtering, soundboard, Voice FX, and the broadcast mix.</li>
    <li><a href={withBase('docs/spotify/')}>Spotify setup</a>: song requests, request filters, and now-playing widgets.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="next-prev">
    <a class="is-prev" href={withBase('docs/')}>
      <p>Back</p>
      <strong>Documentation overview</strong>
    </a>
    <a class="is-next" href={withBase('docs/health-center/')}>
      <p>Next</p>
      <strong>Health Center &rarr;</strong>
    </a>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
